# DOPD of two identical OPDs (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (k), 2026-10-22).  The finding read "DOPD after ZABERR / ZRM
#   reports RMS dOPD = -1.0"; measured, the Zernike commands are not involved: any two identical OPD runs give an
#   all-zero difference map, and RMS2 returns -1 -- its no-nonzero-cell sentinel -- for that (`opd; opd; dopd`
#   read -1.0 too).  DOPD now reports 0 and says why.  Legs: OPD, ZABERR (no save), OPD, DOPD = the brief's
#   sequence; then a perturbed OPD so the difference is real (2.454e-11, the ZABERR_ZRM_DOPD value).  Red on the
#   pre-fix binary (-1.0).
# PIN POLICY (CC 2026-10-23, TO's question): the 3.5664D-11 after the tilt is a RESPONSE (28x the 1.29D-12
#   baseline, which is bounded), so it is pinned to five figures under rule 2 as a deliberate exception to the
#   1e-9 magnitude threshold of rule 1; arm64 shares the five figures (CCMac gate 10).  If arm64 ever moves it,
#   that is a cross-architecture trace difference at 1e-5 relative, worth a finding -- do not widen blindly.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
none
opd 5
zaberr
3
4,5,6
no
opd 5
dopd
perturb 3
global
1e-4,0,0
0,0,0
opd 5
dopd
# EXPECT: RMS dOPD =\s+0\.0+(E\+0+)?\s+\(the two OPDs are identical\)\s+P-V dOPD =\s+0\.0+(E\+0+)?\s+0\.0+(E\+0+)?\s
# EXPECT: RMS OPD error is\s+3\.5664\d*D-11\s+[\s\S]*?RMS dOPD =\s+2\.454\d*E-011
# EXPECT-NOT: RMS dOPD =\s+-1\.0
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
